2026-10-19T22:24:31.1224735Z   ISSUE_NUMBER: 57213
2026-10-19T22:24:31.1225054Z   ISSUE_TITLE: [FEATURE]: Plugin API: change or remove a stored message or part
2026-10-19T22:24:31.1228226Z   ISSUE_BODY: ## Problem

A plugin cannot change a stored message. A plugin cannot remove a stored message or a message part.

## Source (v2.0.31)

- `packages/client/src/effect/api/api.ts:1344` shows the only message operation on the host session API:

  `readonly message: { readonly get: SessionMessageGetOperation<E> }`

  There is no update and no remove.
- `packages/plugin/src/promise/session.ts:153` selects the host operations for plugins. The selection has no `message` entry at all.

## Purpose

A model writes a credential into its own reply. A plugin must remove the credential from the stored reply. A plugin stores a notice, then the notice becomes stale. The plugin must retract the stored notice. The pre-delivery inbox cancel does not help after the host stores the message.

## Proposed minimal API

Add `session.message.update` and `session.message.remove` to the plugin session domain. An update gets a message id and a replacement body or part list. A remove gets a message id.

## What the plugin does today without it

The plugin cannot correct the stored text. The credential stays in the transcript and in the next model request.

